    "created_at": "2023-02-24T13:29:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-24T13:29:14Z",
    "body": "The difference is in the way that an abrupt completion is handled. In ECMAScript, it's simply returned (i.e., the algorithm using `?` returns an abrupt completion), whereas here, its `[[Value]]` is thrown (i.e., the algorithm using `?` throws an Infra-exception). Issue #518 explains the significance of that distinction.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
